<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!--
    CONVERSATION PIECES between a colonist and someone from outside the colony (Source/ColonyCouncil/Outsiders/
    OutsiderTalk.cs runs them, the facts service in Text/Facts/ reads the facts, OutsiderTalkMath.cs chooses and
    Text/Fill.cs fills them). A piece is a short scene said in turn over the two's heads as bubbles: a chat the player
    orders, news of home when asked, getting to know them, and the talks colonists start by themselves. This header
    describes the format for every file in this folder; the same tags and placeholders are there for any text that asks
    the facts service (DESIGN.md, "Facts").

    <ColonyCouncil.OutsiderTalkDef>
      <defName>Rimfolk_OT_Road_Long</defName>   unique, Rimfolk_OT_ and the file's subject
      <topic>road</topic>                         what it's about; the same two drift off a subject they just had
      <uses>chat,home</uses>                      chat (the default), home (asked about their home), know (getting to know
                                                  them); several with commas
      <when>town:far,!tone:sour</when>            conditions, all must hold, in the lines' tag syntax: ! not, | or
      <weight>1</weight>                          optional, 1 by default
      <lines>
        <li>[us] How long were you on the road?</li>          the colonist speaks
        <li>[them,their:tribal] Many sleeps, and cold ones.</li>   the outsider, for a tribe
        <li>[them] Long enough to want a proper bed.</li>      the outsider, anyone else
        <li>[us] Well, you made it.</li>
      </lines>
      <heard>{PEOPLE} are at war with {WAR}.</heard>        optional: added to the town's "Heard lately" once said
      <mark>war</mark><about>WAR</about>                    optional: a mark later talks pick up (talked:war), with the
                                                            fact behind {WAR}, so a callback knows what became of it
    </ColonyCouncil.OutsiderTalkDef>

    THE LINES. [us] is the colonist, [them] the outsider. Lines one after another for the same speaker are choices for
    one turn: the one that fits best is said (more matching tags win), so put the specific ones first and a plain one
    last that is true whenever the piece is. Alternatives of one turn must not contradict each other: when one is for
    kin:you, the plain one says !kin:you. A piece has 2 to 6 turns, the speakers taking turns. Each line is one
    sentence of 90 characters at most (placeholders counted as written), no quotes around it, one "!" at most. Longer
    pieces (5 or 6 turns) for news, their troubles, faith, family and callbacks; 2 or 3 for small talk and passing by.
    A talk in passing runs 3 lines at most, a cool one 3, a sour one 2, a warm one 6.

    HONESTY. A piece is said only when every condition holds and every placeholder in the chosen lines has a value, so
    write each line to be true whenever its conditions are. Never invent a fact the game doesn't hold (a death, a
    battle, a trade): flavour of their ways is fine, a made-up event is not. American spelling, plain and warm, each
    people in its own voice: tribes (the elders, the hunt, moons, spirits, the fire), medieval folk (the reeve, the
    market, the tithe, aye), industrial outlanders (practical, prices, the road, the caravan), spacers (dry, exact),
    the Empire's nobles (formal, the court, honor, titles).

    CONDITIONS (tags; heat in brackets: how current the fact is, so pieces about fresh news are chosen first)
      the moment: spring summer fall winter, morning day evening night, rain snow fog storm clear hot cold; the
        colony's era tribal medieval industrial spacer lowtech, poor rich, small large
      the talk: tone:warm tone:good tone:plain tone:cool tone:sour (a cool or sour chat uses only pieces with a tone:
        condition; any piece with one is said only in that tone); first (never talked) met returning (on a new visit)
        known (familiarity 30) close (60) friends sweethearts lovers; talks:3 talks:8; likesyou coolyou (their regard
        of the colonist) likesus wary (of the colony); did:gift did:meal did:teach did:spar did:duel did:provoke
        did:faith did:court did:letter did:bring; last:TOPIC (their last talk's topic)
      who they are: role:trader role:guest role:lodger role:visitor role:notable role:head role:heir role:envoy;
        them:young (a child: only pieces asking for it) them:old them:hurt them:kind them:abrasive them:leader
        them:married them:widowed them:spousehere them:parent them:smallchild them:childhere them:best:SKILLDEF
        them:outranks (both hold a title, theirs the higher); kin (family of theirs in the colony) kin:you (the
        colonist is that family)
      the colonist: us:young (only pieces asking for it) us:old us:hurt us:newcomer us:leader us:speaker us:noble
        us:doctor us:outranks us:married us:widowed us:spousehere us:parent us:smallchild us:best:SKILLDEF; in a colonist's
        own line also their traits and passions (trait:Kind, trait:Lazy, skill:Cooking) and old teen hurt grieving
        lowmood highmood; in an outsider's own line their traits by name (trait:Greedy, never a degree), old teen
        hurt
      their people: their:tribal their:medieval their:industrial their:spacer their:lowtech their:hightech
        their:empire their:noble their:leader their:rough (a rough outlander union or a fierce tribe, friendly enough
        now) their:ally (allied with the colony) samefaith otherfaith; their:sameage their:behind their:ahead (their
        age beside the colony's: the same, an earlier one, a later one)
      their town: town town:near town:far; home:desert home:frozen home:jungle home:swamp home:forest home:plains
        home:mountains home:hills home:coast home:cold home:hot home:mild; town:head town:notable town:newhead
        town:headdied town:loss town:ill town:letter (a letter under way) town:wrote (one in 20 days) town:site
        town:quest (offered) quest:ongoing (taken on, under way: {QUESTNOW}) town:caravan town:visitors (theirs on
        the way) town:short:food town:short:medicine town:short:hands town:short:fuel
      wars: their:war war:new war:long war:losing (they have fewer towns than when it began) war:winning (the
        enemy has) war:fought (their fighters and the enemy's met on the colony's land) war:ourfoe (their enemy is
        the colony's too) war:ourfriend; their:peace (a war of theirs over in 30 days); world:war (two other
        peoples, new); world:peace (two other peoples made peace in 30 days: {PEACEA} {PEACEB}); battle:here
        battle:theirs (two peoples fought on the colony's land in 10 days)
      the world's events (Rimfolk's world situations): situation situation:theirs situation:bad situation:good
        situation:new situation:long situation:helped situation:sickness :hunger :cold :war :trade :faith
        :politics :empire :disaster :beasts ws:DEFNAME (a name can be a person's, a ship's or a band's: write
        for the one event); situation:ended ended:theirs ended:helped ended:bad (a hard time) ended:ws:DEFNAME
        ended:sickness... ; condition condition:DEFNAME (toxic fallout, a cold snap, a volcanic winter...)
      what the world's history holds lately (30 days): town:lately town:lately:KIND (something at their town, by
        the history's kind and its family: town:lately:world, town:lately:world:taken, town:lately:world:began)
        them:lately them:lately:KIND (something the outsider took part in: them:lately:tie:favour:made)
      ties between the two sides (the colony, its people or one of the colony; the outsider, their people or town):
        tie:favour tie:promise tie:claim tie:debt tie:fealty tie:grudge, each with :ours or :theirs (which side is
        bound: owes, promised, swore, holds the grudge), :you (the colonist is a party to it), :due (asked for now);
        the party it is toward by name: {FAVOURFOR} {PROMISEDTO} {CLAIMON} {DEBTTO} {FEALTYTO} {GRUDGEAGAINST}
      the colony: colony:raid colony:raidby colony:raid:them (their own people) colony:raid:theirfoe
        colony:raid:fallen colony:raid:mechs :insects :animals :tribal :people; colony:death colony:death:battle
        colony:birth colony:wedding colony:newcomer colony:decree colony:election colony:camp colony:harvest
        colony:hungry colony:plenty colony:disaster colony:research colony:project colony:day colony:daytoday
        colony:daysoon colony:daypast colony:traders colony:young colony:old colony:children colony:animals
        colony:prisoners colony:expecting colony:noble (another colonist holds a title: {NOBLE} {NOBLETITLE})
        colony:quiet (no big threat in 30 days) colony:hospital (its hospital has a name: {HOSPITAL}, "hospital" or
        "sickroom") colony:hospital:renowned (known across the region) colony:doctor (the doctor the colony trusts
        most is at home: {DOCTOR}; us:doctor when that's the colonist)
      what their people remember: deed:KIND (released tended gift gaveGift hardship refugees harvestHelp
        killed captured robbed slighted aid taught... see World/FactionMemory.cs) deed:good deed:bad deed:owed
        deedbest:KIND (the good deed {DEEDNAME} and {DEEDBY} come from) wrongbest:KIND ({WRONGNAME}) their:friend
        byyou byyou:freed byyou:tended byyou:helped
      callbacks: talked:KEY (an earlier talk between the two left the mark KEY, half a day ago or more) with what
        became of its fact: then:still then:over then:dead then:changed, and for a quest then:success
        then:failed (a peace: still holds, over broke); then:recent then:long. A piece with a
        talked: or then: condition is a callback: it is weighed with one earlier mark at a time, and {THEN} is what
        that talk was about. A callback about a change settles the mark.

    PLACEHOLDERS: {COLONIST} {OUTSIDER} {COLONY} {PEOPLE} {TOWN} {HOMELAND} (the land, "temperate forest") {SEASON}
      {WEATHER} {LEADER} {LEADERTITLE} {THEIRTITLE} {OURTITLE} {THEIRROLE} {THEIRFAITH} {OURFAITH} {THEIRSKILL}
      {OURSKILL} {THEIRSPOUSE} {THEIRCHILD} {OURSPOUSE} {OURCHILD} {KIN} {KINWORD} (what {KIN} is to them, "sister")
      {HEAD} {HEADTITLE} {NOTABLE} {NOTABLETITLE} {ILL} {ILLTITLE} {LOST} {LOSTTITLE} {OLDHEAD} {WROTE} {WRITER}
      {SITE} {QUEST} {WAR} {PEACEWITH} {WARA} {WARB} {BATTLEA} {BATTLEB} {SITUATION} {SITUATIONPLACE} {ENDED}
      {CONDITION} {COOK} {ARTIST} {OURLEADER} {SPEAKER} {DISASTER} {CAMP} {TRADERS} {NEWCOMER} {DAY} {RAIDERS}
      {DEAD} {BORN} {WEDDING} {DECREE} {RESEARCH} {PROJECT} {DEEDNAME} {DEEDBY} {WRONGNAME} {YOURDEEDNAME}
      {FRIEND} {NOBLE} {NOBLETITLE} {QUESTNOW} {PEACEA} {PEACEB} {HOSPITAL} {DOCTOR} {THEN} {NOW} (who leads now, in a
      then:changed callback) {FAVOURFOR} (who a favour of theirs is owed to) {PROMISEDTO} (who they promised)
      {CLAIMON} (the one of the colony their family has a claim on) {DEBTTO} (whom a debt is owed) {FEALTYTO} (whom
      fealty is sworn) {GRUDGEAGAINST} (whom a grudge is held against). Values that are names keep their case;
      {SITUATION} {ENDED} {SITE} {CONDITION} {DISASTER} come with "the" ("the gray cough"), and a line starting with
      one is capitalized for you.
  -->

  <!-- ================= Greetings, by how well they know each other ================= -->

  <ColonyCouncil.OutsiderTalkDef>
    <defName>Rimfolk_OT_Greet_First</defName>
    <topic>greeting</topic>
    <uses>chat,know</uses>
    <when>first</when>
    <lines>
      <li>[us] I don't think we've met, I'm {COLONIST}.</li>
      <li>[them,their:tribal] I am {OUTSIDER} of {PEOPLE}, and I greet you.</li>
      <li>[them,their:medieval] {OUTSIDER}, of {PEOPLE}, and well met.</li>
      <li>[them,their:empire] {OUTSIDER}, and I travel under the Empire's protection.</li>
      <li>[them] {OUTSIDER}, with {PEOPLE}, good to meet you.</li>
      <li>[us] Welcome to {COLONY}, then.</li>
    </lines>
  </ColonyCouncil.OutsiderTalkDef>

  <ColonyCouncil.OutsiderTalkDef>
    <defName>Rimfolk_OT_Greet_FirstSettlers</defName>
    <topic>greeting</topic>
    <uses>chat,know</uses>
    <when>first,town</when>
    <lines>
      <li>[them] So you're the ones who settled out here.</li>
      <li>[us] We are, this is {COLONY}.</li>
      <li>[them,town:far] I've come a long way from {TOWN} to see it.</li>
      <li>[them,town:near] I'm from {TOWN}, just a short way off.</li>
      <li>[them] I'm from {TOWN}, if you know it.</li>
      <li>[us] Then I hope we'll see more of you.</li>
    </lines>
  </ColonyCouncil.OutsiderTalkDef>

  <ColonyCouncil.OutsiderTalkDef>
    <defName>Rimfolk_OT_Greet_FirstYoungColony</defName>
    <topic>greeting</topic>
    <when>first,colony:young</when>
    <lines>
      <li>[them] You haven't been here long, have you?</li>
      <li>[us] Not long, we're still finding our feet.</li>
      <li>[them,their:tribal] The land takes a while to know a new face.</li>
      <li>[them] It shows, but in a good way.</li>
    </lines>
  </ColonyCouncil.OutsiderTalkDef>

  <ColonyCouncil.OutsiderTalkDef>
    <defName>Rimfolk_OT_Greet_Returning</defName>
    <topic>greeting</topic>
    <uses>chat,know</uses>
    <when>returning,!friends</when>
    <lines>
      <li>[us] {OUTSIDER}, you came back.</li>
      <li>[them,their:tribal] The path led me here again, as I hoped it would.</li>
      <li>[them,their:noble] I said I would return, and I keep my word.</li>
      <li>[them] I said I would, didn't I?</li>
      <li>[us] It's good to see a face we know.</li>
    </lines>
  </ColonyCouncil.OutsiderTalkDef>

  <ColonyCouncil.OutsiderTalkDef>
    <defName>Rimfolk_OT_Greet_ReturningFriend</defName>
    <topic>greeting</topic>
    <uses>chat,know</uses>
    <when>returning,friends</when>
    <lines>
      <li>[them] There you are, {COLONIST}, I was hoping you'd still be here.</li>
      <li>[us] Where else would I be, {OUTSIDER}?</li>
      <li>[them,town] I told them at {TOWN} I'd look in on you.</li>
      <li>[them] I was hoping to find you here.</li>
      <li>[us] Sit down, then, and tell me everything.</li>
      <li>[them] Everything would take a week, but I'll start.</li>
    </lines>
  </ColonyCouncil.OutsiderTalkDef>

  <ColonyCouncil.OutsiderTalkDef>
    <defName>Rimfolk_OT_Greet_Again</defName>
    <topic>greeting</topic>
    <when>met,!returning</when>
    <weight>0.6</weight>
    <lines>
      <li>[them] Back again, {COLONIST}?</li>
      <li>[us,trait:Abrasive] Don't look so pleased about it.</li>
      <li>[us] Couldn't keep away.</li>
    </lines>
  </ColonyCouncil.OutsiderTalkDef>

  <ColonyCouncil.OutsiderTalkDef>
    <defName>Rimfolk_OT_Greet_Morning</defName>
    <topic>greeting</topic>
    <when>morning</when>
    <weight>0.7</weight>
    <lines>
      <li>[us] Morning, did you sleep at all?</li>
      <li>[them,role:guest] Better than I have in weeks, thank you.</li>
      <li>[them,their:tribal] The ground was kind to my back.</li>
      <li>[them] Well enough, thank you.</li>
      <li>[us] Good, it's a long day otherwise.</li>
    </lines>
  </ColonyCouncil.OutsiderTalkDef>

  <ColonyCouncil.OutsiderTalkDef>
    <defName>Rimfolk_OT_Greet_Evening</defName>
    <topic>greeting</topic>
    <when>evening|night</when>
    <weight>0.7</weight>
    <lines>
      <li>[them] Long day for you?</li>
      <li>[us,us:hurt] Long, and I've the bruises to show for it.</li>
      <li>[us] Long enough, how was yours?</li>
      <li>[them] Quiet, which is how I like them.</li>
    </lines>
  </ColonyCouncil.OutsiderTalkDef>

  <ColonyCouncil.OutsiderTalkDef>
    <defName>Rimfolk_OT_Greet_Sweethearts</defName>
    <topic>greeting</topic>
    <uses>chat,know</uses>
    <when>sweethearts|lovers</when>
    <lines>
      <li>[them] I've been counting the days, you know.</li>
      <li>[us] So have I, {OUTSIDER}.</li>
      <li>[them,town:far] {TOWN} is too far from here, that's the trouble.</li>
      <li>[them] Walk with me a while before anyone needs you.</li>
      <li>[us] Gladly.</li>
      <li>[them] Then let's not waste the time we have.</li>
    </lines>
  </ColonyCouncil.OutsiderTalkDef>

  <ColonyCouncil.OutsiderTalkDef>
    <defName>Rimfolk_OT_Greet_Kin</defName>
    <topic>family</topic>
    <uses>chat,know</uses>
    <when>kin</when>
    <weight>1.5</weight>
    <lines>
      <li>[them,kin:you] {COLONIST}, my own {KINWORD}, look at you.</li>
      <li>[them,!kin:you] How is my {KINWORD} {KIN} getting on with you?</li>
      <li>[us,kin:you] It's good to see family, {OUTSIDER}.</li>
      <li>[us,!kin:you] {KIN} is well, and pulls their weight.</li>
      <li>[them,kin:you] Your people at home ask after you.</li>
      <li>[them,!kin:you] Tell {KIN} I asked after them.</li>
    </lines>
  </ColonyCouncil.OutsiderTalkDef>

  <ColonyCouncil.OutsiderTalkDef>
    <defName>Rimfolk_OT_Greet_Noble</defName>
    <topic>greeting</topic>
    <when>their:noble</when>
    <lines>
      <li>[us] We don't see many of your rank out here, {OUTSIDER}.</li>
      <li>[them,their:empire] The Empire sends its own wherever it pleases.</li>
      <li>[them] Out here my title of {THEIRTITLE} counts for little, and I find I like that.</li>
      <li>[us,us:noble] We're both a long way from court.</li>
      <li>[us] Then you're welcome as yourself.</li>
    </lines>
  </ColonyCouncil.OutsiderTalkDef>

  <ColonyCouncil.OutsiderTalkDef>
    <defName>Rimfolk_OT_Greet_Guest</defName>
    <topic>greeting</topic>
    <when>role:guest,met</when>
    <lines>
      <li>[us] Is there anything you need while you're with us?</li>
      <li>[them,them:abrasive] A quieter bed, but I'll manage.</li>
      <li>[them] Nothing at all, you've been kind.</li>
      <li>[us] Say the word if that changes.</li>
    </lines>
  </ColonyCouncil.OutsiderTalkDef>

  <!-- ================= Children ================= -->

  <ColonyCouncil.OutsiderTalkDef>
    <defName>Rimfolk_OT_Young_Visitor</defName>
    <topic>greeting</topic>
    <when>them:young</when>
    <lines>
      <li>[us] Hello there, are you with the grownups?</li>
      <li>[them,town] I'm not little, I came all the way from {TOWN}.</li>
      <li>[them] I'm not little, I walked the whole way.</li>
      <li>[us] All that way, on your own two feet?</li>
      <li>[them] Most of it, anyway.</li>
    </lines>
  </ColonyCouncil.OutsiderTalkDef>

  <ColonyCouncil.OutsiderTalkDef>
    <defName>Rimfolk_OT_Young_Animals</defName>
    <topic>colony</topic>
    <when>them:young,colony:animals</when>
    <lines>
      <li>[them] Are all those animals yours?</li>
      <li>[us] The colony's, and they all have names.</li>
      <li>[them] Can I see them before we go?</li>
      <li>[us] If your people say so.</li>
    </lines>
  </ColonyCouncil.OutsiderTalkDef>

  <ColonyCouncil.OutsiderTalkDef>
    <defName>Rimfolk_OT_Young_Colonist</defName>
    <topic>road</topic>
    <when>us:young</when>
    <lines>
      <li>[us] Are you from far away?</li>
      <li>[them,town:far] From {TOWN}, farther than you've ever been, I'd guess.</li>
      <li>[them,town] From {TOWN}, over that way.</li>
      <li>[them] Far enough to have sore feet.</li>
      <li>[us] What's it like there?</li>
      <li>[them] Different, and you'd want to come home after a week.</li>
    </lines>
  </ColonyCouncil.OutsiderTalkDef>

  <ColonyCouncil.OutsiderTalkDef>
    <defName>Rimfolk_OT_Young_Both</defName>
    <topic>greeting</topic>
    <when>us:young,them:young</when>
    <lines>
      <li>[us] Do you want to see where we hide when it's our turn to do chores?</li>
      <li>[them] Will we get in trouble?</li>
      <li>[us] Only if somebody tells.</li>
    </lines>
  </ColonyCouncil.OutsiderTalkDef>

  <!-- ================= When it goes cool or sour ================= -->

  <ColonyCouncil.OutsiderTalkDef>
    <defName>Rimfolk_OT_Curt_FineDay</defName>
    <topic>weather</topic>
    <when>tone:cool|tone:sour</when>
    <lines>
      <li>[us,rain] Wet one today.</li>
      <li>[us,snow] Cold one today.</li>
      <li>[us,!rain,!snow] Fine day, isn't it?</li>
      <li>[them] If you say so.</li>
    </lines>
  </ColonyCouncil.OutsiderTalkDef>

  <ColonyCouncil.OutsiderTalkDef>
    <defName>Rimfolk_OT_Curt_OwnCounsel</defName>
    <topic>greeting</topic>
    <when>tone:cool|tone:sour</when>
    <lines>
      <li>[us] Anything you'd like to know about the place?</li>
      <li>[them,their:tribal] I will learn what I need with my own eyes.</li>
      <li>[them] I'll keep my own counsel, if it's all the same to you.</li>
      <li>[us] Suit yourself.</li>
    </lines>
  </ColonyCouncil.OutsiderTalkDef>

  <ColonyCouncil.OutsiderTalkDef>
    <defName>Rimfolk_OT_Curt_Want</defName>
    <topic>greeting</topic>
    <when>tone:sour</when>
    <lines>
      <li>[them] Is there something you want?</li>
      <li>[us] Only a word.</li>
    </lines>
  </ColonyCouncil.OutsiderTalkDef>

  <ColonyCouncil.OutsiderTalkDef>
    <defName>Rimfolk_OT_Curt_Road</defName>
    <topic>road</topic>
    <when>tone:cool</when>
    <lines>
      <li>[us] Was the road kind to you?</li>
      <li>[them] Kind enough, I won't keep you.</li>
      <li>[us] Right, then.</li>
    </lines>
  </ColonyCouncil.OutsiderTalkDef>

  <ColonyCouncil.OutsiderTalkDef>
    <defName>Rimfolk_OT_Curt_Smoke</defName>
    <topic>colony</topic>
    <when>tone:cool|tone:sour,colony:raid</when>
    <lines>
      <li>[them] I heard you had a fight here.</li>
      <li>[us] We did, and we're still standing.</li>
      <li>[them] For now.</li>
    </lines>
  </ColonyCouncil.OutsiderTalkDef>

  <ColonyCouncil.OutsiderTalkDef>
    <defName>Rimfolk_OT_Curt_Grudge</defName>
    <topic>deeds</topic>
    <when>tone:cool|tone:sour,deed:bad</when>
    <lines>
      <li>[them] My people haven't forgotten what yours did.</li>
      <li>[us] I'd hoped that was behind us.</li>
      <li>[them] It isn't.</li>
    </lines>
  </ColonyCouncil.OutsiderTalkDef>

  <ColonyCouncil.OutsiderTalkDef>
    <defName>Rimfolk_OT_Curt_Abrasive</defName>
    <topic>greeting</topic>
    <when>tone:cool|tone:sour,them:abrasive</when>
    <lines>
      <li>[us] You look like you could use some company.</li>
      <li>[them] I look like I'd like to be left alone, and I would.</li>
    </lines>
  </ColonyCouncil.OutsiderTalkDef>

  <ColonyCouncil.OutsiderTalkDef>
    <defName>Rimfolk_OT_Curt_Trade</defName>
    <topic>trade</topic>
    <when>tone:cool|tone:sour,role:trader</when>
    <lines>
      <li>[us] Good trading so far?</li>
      <li>[them] I'll tell you when I've counted it.</li>
    </lines>
  </ColonyCouncil.OutsiderTalkDef>

</Defs>
